# Cache-Control for the share card, and nothing else.
#
# The card is not fingerprinted the way /assets/* is, and scrapers cache hard.
# A day is long enough to be free and short enough that replacing the card
# actually lands.
#
# Deliberately no /assets/* rule here, and no `immutable`. _headers matches by
# request path, so an immutable rule would stamp a year onto the reply for an
# asset that is not there -- and this site answers an unmatched path with
# index.html and a 200, by design (see the deployment notes in README.md). The
# edge would then serve cached HTML under a JavaScript filename for a year. The
# sibling `borderline` repo can carry that rule because it ships a 404.html,
# which turns a missing asset back into a 404; this repo must never have one,
# because that same file is what would disable the fallback /portfolio and
# /resume rely on.
#
# This file is not _redirects. It decorates responses after routing and does not
# affect matching, which is why it is safe here at all.
/og.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400
